**Marcus Aurelius — 33/100 — PASS** (entity-gap model). Packet saved to `docs/content-analysis/entity-gaps/Marcus-Aurelius.md`.

He's `inProgress` in the backlog right now (started 06:00 today, stage 0.5 log is empty), and no 9takes page exists — so this was a create-or-skip call.

**Why it fails the model:** the exact-name SERP is the most fortified this command has audited. Wikipedia (plus two spin-out articles), Britannica, Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, HISTORY, Biography.com, Yale UP, EBSCO, Birley's academic biography — *and* Daily Stoic, which owns the popular self-help register 9takes would otherwise compete in. Seven-plus dedicated biographies, no catalyst (nearest are ~2 years stale: Robertson's Yale bio and *Gladiator II*), zero local GSC demand. Scores 53 raw, −20 Wikipedia-fortress penalty.

**Why it's still worth writing anyway** — two findings that make this packet more than a rejection:

1. **The typology long-tail is wide open.** `marcus aurelius personality type` / `enneagram type` returns sakinorva, personality-database, Boo, getpersonality, personalitylist, a Blogspot socionics post. No authoritative owner. That's the only winnable lane, and it's the backlog's actual rationale.

2. **There's a genuinely ownable contradiction the Stoicism industry doesn't lead with.** The Fronto correspondence is a second, independent first-person archive — warm, anxious, complaining about the cold in his bedroom, lying awake dreading what he'd said in the Senate. *Meditations* isn't a portrait of a serene man; it's the reps he was still running against that temperament decades later, in private, never published. **He never published the manual, and he never finished needing it.**

**The thing I'd flag hardest:** `Ryan-Holiday.md` is already drafted as Enneagram 1, titled *"The Rule He Can't Keep,"* with Marcus in its `knows_about` — and these two are meant to be a linked cluster. Holiday's essay is hypocrisy-shaped (preaches a rule, caught on camera breaking it). Marcus's must be the opposite shape, because he taught no one and had no audience. If the draft writes "but privately, he was a hypocrite," it has collapsed into the Holiday essay. The packet says so explicitly so Gate 6 doesn't catch it late.

Also loaded the packet with the traps: don't call him a hypochondriac (those complaints in *Ad M. Caes.* book 5 are largely **Fronto's** — easiest load-bearing error to make here), Faustina's gossip is *Historia Augusta*/Dio and can't be stated as fact, death location is disputed, and every quote needs a book-and-section pin because circulating "Marcus Aurelius quotes" are heavily fabricated.

